{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, round-trip via rebar-status labels)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStatus mapping is hardcoded: outbound reads built-in `value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` at\n**four** consumer sites (Scope), mirrored as `config.local_to_jira_status`; inbound inverts\nbuilt-in `config.jira_to_local_status` and prefers the `rebar-status:<local>` label, hardcoded\nto `blocked`/`cancelled` (`outbound_labels._STATUS_ANNOTATION_LABEL`). A project lacking a rebar\nstatus has no echo-safe remap; a collapse over other statuses has no label. Status must become\nconfig-driven on the S1 core: always **map-or-drift** (never skip); any remap/collapse must\nround-trip via `rebar-status:`.\n\n## Dependency (prerequisite ticket)\n\nWires the status axis onto the S1 mapping core **[rebar:bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141]** (on `main`).\n`mapping_config` provides `load_mapping_config(root=None)` and\n`resolve_for_project(config, project_key, *, builtin) -> MappingLayer` (merges\n`builtin ← [mapping.default] ← [mapping.projects.<KEY>]`) with `MappingLayer.status_map`\n(resolved local→Jira; `SKIP` = drop; ABSENT = drift). `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` is the `builtin`,\nso with no `[mapping]` config the effective map = today's default — behaviour and parity tests\nunchanged.\n\n## Approach — one FORWARD seam; inbound stays reverse-map-free\n\nOnly **outbound (forward)** becomes per-project. Inbound needs no reverse map/project key: the\n`rebar-status:` label makes every non-built-in status self-describing (see 4).\n\n1. **`config.py` — forward resolution entry point.** Add\n   `effective_status_map(project_key, root=None) -> dict[str,str]` = `load_mapping_config` +\n   `resolve_for_project(builtin=LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA)`. The literal stays the built-in fallback\n   (lock-step with `value_maps` via the parity test); `mapping_config` imported LAZILY (config.py\n   stays stdlib-only at top level). NO reverse resolution added.\n\n2. **Outbound consumers read the resolved map.** Project key resolved once per ticket in\n   `outbound_differ` (where `projects_store.resolve_project(ticket, mapping)` already runs),\n   threaded to mappers as optional `status_map: dict|None` (`None` → built-in fallback). Sites:\n   `outbound_mapper.map_fields_to_remote` (shared UPDATE, Cloud+DC),\n   `jira/outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (Cloud CREATE), `jira_datacenter/backend`\n   create, `jira/acli` transition name.\n\n3. **Drift = leave Jira as-is, never a per-mutation failure.** Decided ONLY in the mapper: with\n   no entry for a local status it **omits the `status` field** (rebar keeps its status; Jira\n   unchanged) + records a drift alert — replacing today's `.get(status,\"To Do\")` coerce.\n   `reconcile_helpers.preflight_status_mapping` needs NO change: it runs AFTER the mapper\n   (`reconcile.py:485`), so a drifted mutation carries no `status` field (preflight's\n   skip-when-no-status branch makes it non-offending) and mapped mutations carry the Jira NAME\n   it already tolerates. Kill-switch untouched.\n\n4. **Generalised `rebar-status:` round-trip (built-in-reverse stamp rule).** Outbound\n   (`outbound_labels`): replace hardcoded blocked/cancelled stamping with stamp\n   `rebar-status:<local>` **iff `_BUILTIN_JIRA_TO_LOCAL.get(status_map[local]) != local`**\n   (`.get`, never subscript — no KeyError). On the built-in map this selects exactly\n   {blocked, cancelled} (in_progress/closed are canonical preimages; `deleted` never reaches\n   stamping via `outbound_differ excluded_statuses={archived,deleted}`) — default stamping\n   bit-for-bit preserved. Under ANY config remap/collapse, every status whose Jira target isn't\n   the built-in canonical name for `<local>` is labelled → inbound recovers it from the label\n   WITHOUT a reverse map. A DRIFTED status has no target → no label. Inbound (parse-helper\n   sites): recover by **parsing the `rebar-status:<local>` suffix**, validating `<local>`\n   against the local-status vocabulary (a constant — no config/project key), via one shared\n   helper; the plain `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.get()` built-in fallback is correct because every\n   non-built-in status arrives labelled. Precedence unchanged. Malformed `[mapping]` fails\n   closed via S1's `MappingConfigError`.\n\n5. **Fetcher known-set widened (no false alarms).** `fetcher._known_jira_statuses` today reads\n   only built-in `config.jira_to_local_status` keys → a config-only status trips a spurious \"no\n   reconciler mapping\" warning. Widen it to built-in ∪ every Jira status NAME declared across\n   config (`status_map` values + declared `statuses`, loaded from `repo_root`); empty-map\n   kill-switch preserved. A superset for warning suppression, no per-project threading.\n\n6. **Parity preserved.** `value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` / `config.local_to_jira_status` stay\n   the built-in literal (injected as `builtin`), so parity tests stay green.\n\n## Scope (files)\n\n- `config.py` — `effective_status_map` (forward only, lazy `mapping_config`).\n- `outbound_differ.py` — resolve project key once; thread `status_map` to mappers + label diff.\n- `adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py` — optional `status_map`; drift-omit; built-in fallback.\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — CREATE reads effective map.\n- `adapters/jira/acli.py` — transition name via effective map.\n- `outbound_labels.py` — built-in-reverse stamp rule from the effective forward map.\n- `inbound_fields.py` — generalised `rebar-status:<local>` label recovery (shared helper); plain built-in reverse unchanged.\n- `inbound_translate.py` / `apply_inbound_events.py` / `inbound_differ.py` — shared parse helper (retire `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL`).\n- `applier.py` — re-export the shared helper in `__all__`.\n- `fetcher.py` — widen `_known_jira_statuses` to built-in ∪ config-declared Jira status names.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit** — translation is pure over the resolved map. Tests hit REAL entry\npoints (`config.effective_status_map`, the outbound mappers,\n`outbound_labels._diff_status_annotation_labels`, `inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields`,\n`fetcher._known_jira_statuses`).\n\n- **Config-effect:** `status_map` `blocked→\"To Do\"` → outbound targets `To Do`; no override →\n  built-in. `test_status_config_effect`.\n- **Drift:** unmapped status → mapper omits `status` (+ stderr), not crash/coerce.\n  `test_unmapped_status_drifts`.\n- **Remap/collapse round-trip:** a config remap AND a collapse over a NON blocked/cancelled\n  status stamp `rebar-status:<local>`; inbound recovers each via the label.\n  `test_status_remap_roundtrip`/`test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- **Fetcher no-false-alarm:** a config-only status is in `_known_jira_statuses` → no warning.\n  `test_fetcher_known_includes_config`.\n- **Parity:** `value_maps`↔`config` parity tests stay green.\n\n**Rollback:** config-gated — no `[mapping]` ⇒ effective map = built-in (drift unreachable, stamp\nrule = {blocked,cancelled}, fetcher known-set = built-in); label FORMAT unchanged, back-out is a\nplain revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective forward map = `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>` via S1\n  `resolve_for_project`; a non-default overlay changes the outbound target through the real\n  mapper path — `test_status_config_effect`.\n- [ ] An unmapped status **drifts**: the outbound mutation omits `status` (Jira unchanged) + a\n  non-fatal drift warning; never skipped nor a per-mutation failure — `test_unmapped_status_drifts`.\n- [ ] A config remap AND a collapsed pair (OTHER than blocked/cancelled) round-trip losslessly\n  via `rebar-status:<local>` labels, recovered inbound without a reverse map —\n  `test_status_remap_roundtrip`, `test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- [ ] A config-only Jira status name is known to the fetcher (no spurious unmapped-status\n  warning) — `test_fetcher_known_includes_config`.\n- [ ] The `value_maps`↔`config` parity tests in `state/test_config.py` stay green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787334695295407001,"uuid":"fd755c28-277d-4cf3-9436-e300abbd4b51"}